-- title:
--   On each isotypic component of commuting subgroups, one factor has a small-degree identity kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite group, $V$ a finite-dimensional complex inner product space with $\dim V>0$, and $\rho$ a representation of $G$ on $V$ that is unitary: $\langle\rho(g)x,\rho(g)y\rangle=\langle x,y\rangle$ for all $g\in G$ and $x,y\in V$. Let $b\ge1$ and let $H_1,\dots,H_b$ be subgroups of $G$ whose elements commute across different indices: $gk=kg$ whenever $i\neq j$, $g\in H_i$ and $k\in H_j$. Let $J$ be the subgroup generated by $H_1,\dots,H_b$ and $\rho_J$ the restriction of $\rho$ to $J$. Let $C\subseteq V$ be an isotypic component of $\rho_J$: for some irreducible $J$-invariant subspace $S\subseteq V$, $C$ is the sum of all $J$-invariant subspaces of $V$ that are isomorphic to $S$ as representations of $J$.
--
--   Then there exist an index $i\in\{1,\dots,b\}$, a natural number $d$ and a function $k:H_i\to\mathbb{C}$ such that
--
--   $$
--   d\le(\dim V)^{1/b},\qquad \sum_{h\in H_i}|k(h)|^2=\frac{d^2}{|H_i|},\qquad k(h^{-1})=\overline{k(h)}\ \ (h\in H_i),
--   $$
--
--   and
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{h\in H_i}k(h)\,\rho(h)x=x\qquad\text{for all }x\in C.
--   $$
--
--   In words: on every isotypic component of the group generated by commuting factors, at least one factor $H_i$ admits a kernel with $\ell^2$-mass $d^2/|H_i|$ for some $d\le(\dim V)^{1/b}$ whose Fourier transform acts as the identity on the component. Together with a criterion turning such a kernel into the statement that the projection onto small-degree types of $H_i$ fixes the component, this covers $V$ by small-degree projections of the factors, the key step of the Hilbert–Schmidt estimate for functions with coset caps on commuting block subgroups.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $J$ is `⨆ i, H i`, and $C$ is `componentSpace (ρ.comp J.subtype) c` for `c` in Mathlib's `isotypicComponents` of the $\mathbb{C}[J]$-module `(ρ.comp J.subtype).asModule`, viewed as a complex subspace of $V$. The root is the real power `(finrank ℂ V : ℝ) ^ (1 / (b : ℝ))`, and the last condition reads `complexFourier (ρ.comp (H i).subtype) k x = x`, where `complexFourier σ k = ∑ g, k g • σ g`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/RepresentationTheory/PartialPermutation/JointKernels.lean#L80-L137

